AI Assist chat
==============

Open AI Assist in gschem. The Chat tab uses the current page's live edit
buffer, including unsaved changes. It never saves or applies a model reply
to the schematic. The existing Schematic text and Design and SPICE tabs are
still available for inspection; each Send refreshes them.

Choose Ollama, OpenAI, DeepSeek, OpenRouter or Other compatible. Select Load
Models, then choose a chat-capable model from the editable dropdown. You can
also type a model ID. Provider endpoints and model choices are remembered
separately in the user's geda-ai/ai-assist.ini under the GLib user config
directory. Endpoints are editable, including for remote Ollama servers.
Model lists may include non-chat models; a model must support the selected
provider's chat API. Nothing downloads a model automatically.

Credentials
-----------

Hosted providers require their own keys:

  OpenAI:     OPENAI_API_KEY
  DeepSeek:   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY (or existing DEEPSEEK_API)
  OpenRouter: OPENROUTER_API_KEY (or OPENROUTER_API)
  Ollama:     optional OLLAMA_API_KEY
  Other:      optional GEDA_AI_API_KEY

Resolution order is the masked API key field, the selected provider's
environment variables, then its key in the specified .env file. A blank
.env path uses .env in the application's current working directory.
An explicit missing file or missing required key is reported in Chat;
enter a path or key and retry. Switching providers clears the typed key.
Keys are not written into preferences, the transcript, argv, or the schematic.
The .env reader accepts KEY=value, single/double quotes, export and comments;
it never executes shell substitutions or changes the process environment.

Enter a question and press Enter or Send. The chosen server receives the
latest schematic and report plus successful earlier turns. Only the latest
snapshot is included as current context. Switching schematic pages starts
a new conversation. New chat clears history manually. The dialog remains
responsive during requests. Cancel or closing the dialog terminates its
helper process; failed/cancelled requests do not enter conversation history.
Provider/model settings cannot change during an outstanding request.

Build and verification
----------------------

The GTK dialog uses GIO subprocess communication and the configured Python
interpreter. gedai/chat_backend.py uses Python's standard library only.
Install it into the same versioned GEDADATADIR as the rest of the runtime:

  make -C gedai install-data
  make -C gschem/src check

The backend tests simulate provider HTTP responses and credentials. The GTK
integration test exercises the real controls and async pipes using an isolated
fixture helper/config directory; it skips if no GTK display is available.
The optional real loopback HTTP test needs permission to bind a local port:

  python3 tests/test_ai_chat_http.py

Protocol references:
  https://docs.ollama.com/api/chat
  https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/chat-completions/overview
  https://api-docs.deepseek.com/api/list-models/
  https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/chat/create-a-chat-completion
  https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/models/list-all-models-and-their-properties
